## 4. Bugs Ranger keeps having — do not write them again

This section is derived from actual fix commits. Ranger's policy engine, plugin and matcher objects
are **constructed once and then read concurrently by every authorization request thread**, in a
process that runs for months. The same five mistakes account for a large share of the "intermittent
failure" / "NPE" / "CME" JIRAs. Check your diff against each one.

### 4.1 Read a mutable shared field **once**, into a local

A field that another thread can replace (`policyEngine`, a `static volatile` plugin instance, a
cache reference) must be copied to a local at the top of the method. Reading it twice means the
second read can see `null` or a different object.

```java
// WRONG - policyEngine can be replaced between the check and the use
public Long getPolicyVersion() {
    return this.policyEngine == null ? -1L : this.policyEngine.getPolicyVersion();
}

// RIGHT - RangerBasePlugin.getPolicyVersion(), after RANGER-5185
public Long getPolicyVersion() {
    RangerPolicyEngine policyEngine = this.policyEngine;

    return policyEngine == null ? -1L : policyEngine.getPolicyVersion();
}
```

Same fix in `RangerOzoneAuthorizer` (RANGER-5247): `if (rangerPlugin == null)` followed by five more
uses of `rangerPlugin` became `RangerBasePlugin plugin = rangerPlugin;` then `plugin` throughout.

**Rule:** if a field is `volatile`, `static`, or reassigned by a refresher/loader thread, the method
gets one local copy and uses only that.

### 4.2 Never lazily initialize a shared field without synchronization

`if (field == null) { field = compute(); }` inside an object shared across request threads is a data
race. It produced `ConcurrentModificationException` during policy evaluation (RANGER-5115) and
intermittent HDFS authorization failures (RANGER-5403).

Two accepted fixes, in order of preference:

**(a) Compute eagerly in the constructor and make the field `final`** — preferred when the
computation is cheap. This is what RANGER-5403 did to `RangerPathResourceMatcher` /
`RangerURLResourceMatcher`:

```java
RecursiveMatcher(String value, Map<String, String> options, char levelSeparatorChar) {
    super(value, options);

    this.levelSeparatorChar = levelSeparatorChar;

    if (this.value == null || getNeedsDynamicEval()) {
        valueWithoutSeparator = null;
        valueWithSeparator    = null;
    } else {
        valueWithoutSeparator = getStringToCompare(this.value);
        valueWithSeparator    = valueWithoutSeparator + levelSeparatorChar;
    }
}
```

**(b) Double-checked locking with a local `ret`** — when the computation is expensive. This is
`RangerAbstractPolicyItemEvaluator.computeWithImpliedGrants()` after RANGER-5115:

```java
protected RangerPolicyItem computeWithImpliedGrants() {
    RangerPolicyItem ret = withImpliedGrants;

    if (ret == null) {
        synchronized (this) {
            ret = withImpliedGrants;

            if (ret == null) {
                ret = ...;            // compute

                withImpliedGrants = ret;
            }
        }
    }

    return ret;
}
```

And the **call sites** stop caching into the shared field themselves — they take a local:

```java
// WRONG (pre-RANGER-5115) - every caller races to populate the shared field
if (withImpliedGrants == null) {
    withImpliedGrants = computeWithImpliedGrants();
}

// RIGHT
RangerPolicyItem withImpliedGrants = computeWithImpliedGrants();
```

**Rule:** in any object reachable from the policy engine, a mutable instance field is a defect
unless it is guarded. Prefer `final` + constructor initialization.

### 4.3 `!= null` is not a validity check for a configured string

`RANGER-5384`: Solr requests were sent with an empty basic-auth header because the code checked
`username != null && password != null`. An unset property is very often `""`, not `null`.

```java
// WRONG
if (username != null && password != null) {

// RIGHT
if (StringUtils.isNotBlank(username) && StringUtils.isNotBlank(password)) {
```

Apply defaults at the point of assignment, not at each use — `RANGER-5010` fixed a validity-schedule
timezone bug this way:

```java
this.timeZone = StringUtils.isNotBlank(timeZone) ? timeZone : "GMT";
```

**Rule:** for any value that came from a config file, a REST payload or a DB column, use
`StringUtils.isNotBlank` / `isNotEmpty`, `CollectionUtils.isNotEmpty`, `MapUtils.isNotEmpty`.
Never a bare `!= null`, and never `.size() > 0`.

### 4.4 Do not build values out of untrusted/parsed text without a guard

`RANGER-5442` replaced `Long.valueOf(appDataVersionJson.get(APP_DATA_ENTRY_VERSION)) + 1L` with:

```java
String versionStr     = appDataVersionJson.get(APP_DATA_ENTRY_VERSION);
long   appDataVersion = StringUtils.isNotBlank(versionStr) ? (Long.parseLong(versionStr) + 1L) : 1L;
```

The same commit replaced `new Gson().fromJson(...)` / `new Gson().toJson(...)` with
`JsonUtils.jsonToMapStringString(...)` / `JsonUtils.mapToJson(...)`.

**Rule:** parse through `org.apache.ranger.authorization.utils.JsonUtils`; never instantiate `Gson`
or `ObjectMapper` at a call site. Guard every `valueOf`/`parseLong`/`parseInt` on parsed text.

### 4.5 Loops that follow a chain must advance the variable they test

`RANGER-4956` — "fixed dedup tags to address potential infinite loop". The update expression re-read
the *original* key instead of the one just assigned:

```java
// WRONG - re-reads replacedIds.get(tagId) forever
for (Long replacerTagId = replacedIds.get(tagId); replacerTagId != null; replacerTagId = replacedIds.get(tagId)) {
    tagId = replacerTagId;
}

// RIGHT
final Long tagId       = listIter.next();
Long       mappedTagId = null;

for (Long replacerTagId = replacedIds.get(tagId); replacerTagId != null; replacerTagId = replacedIds.get(mappedTagId)) {
    mappedTagId = replacerTagId;
}
```

The same commit also stopped inserting **identity mappings** into the replacement map
(`} else if (!tagId.equals(cachedTag.left))`) — a self-mapping is a one-element cycle.

**Rule:** when following a replacement/alias chain, the update expression must read the variable the
body assigned, and the map must never contain `k -> k`.

### 4.6 Other recurring defects

| Defect | Fixed in | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| `LoggerFactory.getLogger(WrongClass.class)` copy-pasted into a new class | RANGER-5017 | The `LOG` class literal must match the enclosing class. |
| Return value of a helper discarded — `add(accessPerms, x);` where `add` returns the (possibly new) collection | RANGER-5115 | Assign it back: `accessPerms = add(accessPerms, x);`. |
| A method's last expression computed but not returned — `Collections.singleton(principal.getName());` then `return null;` | RANGER-5017 | Never leave a bare expression statement that has no side effect. |
| `PrivilegedAction` in `UserGroupInformation.doAs()` swallows checked exceptions | RANGER-4891 | Use `MiscUtil.executePrivilegedAction((PrivilegedExceptionAction<T>) () -> …)`. |
| Builder chain applied to possibly-null args (`.withStartTime(fromDate.getTime())`) | RANGER-5017 | Null-guard each optional element before adding it to the chain. |
| Unused instance member kept alive per authorizer instance | RANGER-5247 | If a value is used only inside one method, it is a local, not a field. |
| Eagerly copying collections in model setters | RANGER-4787 | Use `nullSafeList/Set/Map(...)` in setters and `getUpdatableList/Set/Map(...)` in `addXxx()` — see `RangerBaseModelObject` (§6.2). |
| Redundant condition — `other.itemId != null \|\| !itemId.equals(other.itemId)` | RANGER-5017 | Simplify; do not leave a clause that can never change the result. |

### 4.7 Do not need a follow-up commit

`git log` shows a long tail of `… - #2`, `fix for PMD violation in previous commit`,
`missed in earlier commit`, `fix unit test failure caused by previous fix` — ~70 such commits, most
of them avoidable. Before pushing:

- run the **full** `mvn -T 8 clean verify`, not just the module you touched;
- grep for every other caller of a method whose signature or behaviour you changed;
- if you added a constant/enum/`SearchFilter` key, grep for the switch/map/list it must also be
  registered in (RANGER-4542 was exactly this);
- if you removed a method, check no other module still calls it (RANGER-5324 needed a third commit
  for this).

