## 7. Anti-patterns — reject these in your own diff

**Concurrency / correctness (§4)**

| # | Anti-pattern | Ref |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Reading a `volatile`/shared field more than once in a method | RANGER-5185, RANGER-5247 |
| 2 | `if (field == null) { field = compute(); }` on a shared object | RANGER-5115, RANGER-5403 |
| 3 | A non-`final` instance field on an object reachable from the policy engine | §4.2 |
| 4 | `x != null` as a validity check on a config/REST/DB string | RANGER-5384 |
| 5 | `Long.valueOf(...)` / `parseInt(...)` on parsed text without a guard | RANGER-5442 |
| 6 | `new Gson()` / `new ObjectMapper()` at a call site | RANGER-5442 |
| 7 | Chain-following loop whose update expression re-reads the original key | RANGER-4956 |
| 8 | `LOG` initialized with another class's literal | RANGER-5017 |
| 9 | Discarding the return of a helper that may return a new collection | RANGER-5115 |
| 10 | `PrivilegedAction` inside `UserGroupInformation.doAs()` | RANGER-4891 |
| 11 | Eagerly copying collections in model setters instead of `nullSafeList`/`getUpdatableList` | RANGER-4787 |
| 12 | Instance field used by exactly one method | RANGER-5247 |

