## 8. Responding to review

- Address **every** comment — with a code change or a reply explaining why not. Silent force-pushes
  over open threads stall a PR.
- When a reviewer proposes a concrete alternative (often a code block, sometimes an attached
  `.patch`), take it or explain precisely why it doesn't work. Those suggestions are usually the
  final shape the committer intends to merge.
- Push fixes as new commits during review; don't rewrite history mid-review.
- "This is a nit" is not a category here — rename requests are expected to be applied.
- Re-run `mvn -T 8 clean verify` after every review round.

